 horrible people that do  very violent things they're let out of  prison every  day in this country unfortunately  and that's very scary for us  and victims want to be able to protect  themselves but  here's a scenario perhaps you've not  thought of which absolutely terrifies me  when my stalker my husband's murderer is  released one day  what would prevent him from taking out a  red flag  on me to purposefully disarm me  so that he can harm me that's terrifying  that's just something to think about  well thank you miss collins johnson for  having  the courage to be here and allowing your  story to be told  and and ms goser thank you for speaking  on her behalf and on behalf of so many  victims of violence  thank you uh thank you thank you senator  cruz you know i'm struck  as we come to the end of this hearing by  the points of agreement  perhaps unintentional ms gosur  your point about people who have mental  illness  perhaps  being reluctant to talk to friends or  professionals  is exactly the point that senator durbin  made  i don't know whether you recall but he  said  people should not be  separated from firearms simply because  they have a mental illness  it's dangerous it's risk  it's potential harm to others  that murderer would have no basis  none for going to a judge  and saying nikki gosur  is dangerous a risk of harm to anyone  on the contrary and likewise senator  cruz and i  are both federalists i was a state  attorney general for way longer than  i've been a united states senator  i believe in states rights  to enforce their own laws and need to  make their own laws  and that is the whole purpose of our  proposed  red flag statue  not only to encourage states to make  their own laws but to make them  better so when they do pass their laws  they look more like  thanks to mr koppel for his compliment  to connecticut  more like connecticut than say one of  the other states that  he found less protective  of constitutional rights if they're  going to be 